💡 **SUGGESTION: `_testConfig` duplicates the private config in `confluence_test_support.dart`**

```dart
const _testConfig = {
  'CONFLUENCE_BASE_PATH': 'https://confluence.example.com/wiki',
  'CONFLUENCE_EMAIL': 'dev@example.com',
  'CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN': 'tok-123',
};
```

The comment says it "mirrors `confluence_test_support._testConfig`, which is private" — the values will drift independently when the shared fixture changes (e.g. a new required credential). Consider exporting the shared map (or a `mockConfluenceV2`-style helper) from `confluence_test_support.dart` instead of copying it, so both fixture builders read one source of truth.

